    "summary": "Preflight does not bound complete non-content JSON metadata before loading file payloads. The approximately 120 MiB files_bytes allowance plus ignored unknown object keys permits a stored/corrupt retained file with a large extra JSON value to pass SQL shape/content/path/version bounds; verifier ignores that key and only validates statementCount after loading. The subsequent SELECT/JSON parse can materialize close to the full 120 MiB per release.",
    "impact": "Request-time memory/CPU amplification on malformed or corrupted retained records; fails bounded metadata-before-payload acceptance.",
    "required_correction": "Bound complete encoded non-content metadata before payload SELECT while preserving compatible historical fields; validate statementCount shape/range in the scalar preflight; test oversized extra metadata in both base and candidate slots with complete no-write snapshots; then rerun exact-head QA/security."
  },
